## What I practised
- **Modelling:** [e.g. extrude, loop cuts, scaling, proportional editing]
- **Modifiers:** [e.g. Subdivision Surface for smooth shapes]
- **Materials:** [e.g. colours, roughness, icing and donut shaders]
- **Lighting and camera:** [e.g. positioning lights and the camera]
- **Rendering:** [e.g. Eevee or Cycles, resolution, saving the image]
- **Export one as `.fbx` and import it into Unity

## How this connects to my goal
Hazard objects for the VR scene (a rug, a spill, a cup on the floor)
will be modelled in Blender. The coffee/cup part of this tutorial is
the closest practice to that.

